  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="78b009bc-6513-56d3-af48-bf750a869495" activityNameId="73e58d4e-9d0f-5b94-8a76-a0e8f4fe8be4" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Mechanical treatment plant, WEEE scrap</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Mechanical treatment plant, WEEE scrap
The functional unit represents a site for the mechanical treatment of WEEE devices (including the preceding manual depollution step), with all the necessary facilities. Process data based on own estimations, using proper experiences within the Swiss e-Waste systems. The here described plant has an assumed treatment capacity of 50’000 t per year over a time span of 25 years. Update 2023: The bill of materials is assumed to remain the same, but the background datasets are updating using new ICT datasets.; Geography: This module is based on experiences in Switzerland as a proxy for the global situation.; UUID: 4d3f2267-79d2-37be-aead-51e2c96b173f
This module includes land use, buildings and facilities (machinery, cables, etc.) as well as the respective disposal activities of a plant for mechanical WEEE treatment.
Location: This module is based on experiences in Switzerland as a proxy for the global situation.
Technology: Modern mechanical treatment plant, based on information from literature &amp; proper knowledge about companies in Switzerland
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: 
Sampling: Literature &amp; own estimations
Extrapolations: see Geography and Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_4d3f2267-79d2-37be-aead-51e2c96b173f.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
